Subject: Record the array element kind at each element access site

What this does
  At every array element load and store, records the kind of the value (int32,
  float64, object or mixed, and whether a hole was in the way) on the access
  site's per-instruction record, as an `elem=` field on its `P` line.

Why we need it
  An elements kind lets compiled code drop the tag guard on an element read and
  lets the profile seed the kind at allocation. Nothing recorded it.

What it adds
  `AOT_ELEM_*`, `JSAotProfPc.elem_kinds`, `js_aot_prof_elem` and the `elem=`
  field; `profmerge.py` merges it and fixes the per-instruction record, which
  was not being merged at all.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

